## FRESH MONEY TEST
**Fresh money allocation: 7%**

The gap between 7% (fresh money) and 12% (recommended maximum) reflects the following: a fresh buyer has no embedded gain to protect and faces the full downside of a $160M micro-cap with no forward guidance, a CEO who is simultaneously the IR function, a single analyst covering the stock (one question on the Q&A), and a growth strategy that is vision-level rather than plan-level. The turnaround is real, but a fresh buyer is paying for future execution that has not yet been demonstrated beyond cost-cutting. The 5-point gap is not inertia — it is the appropriate discount for entering a story where the hard part (growth) has not yet begun.

